From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: find a non-AP MLD by its link address for a frame
 from an unknown STA

mac80211 translates the addresses of a frame of a non-AP MLD to the
MLD addresses only where it finds the station. Without a driver
station, for example in the short time while hostapd removes and adds
the station again for a new association, it reports a Data frame with
the link address of the non-AP MLD. ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown() looks
that address up with ap_get_sta(), which knows the non-AP MLD only by
its MLD address, and sends a Disassociation or Deauthentication with
reason 7 to a station that is associated.

Where ap_get_sta() finds no station on a link of an AP MLD, look the
station up by its link address. The rules for the station found stay
as they are, and a sender that hostapd does not hold still gets the
frame.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -9621,6 +9621,12 @@ void ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown(struct h
 	struct sta_info *sta;
 
 	sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, src);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/* Without a driver station, the frame of a non-AP MLD keeps the
+	 * address of its link */
+	if (!sta && hapd->conf->mld_ap)
+		sta = ap_get_link_sta(hapd, src);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	if (sta &&
 	    ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC) ||
 	     ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK) && wds))) {
